```coq
(* Type class definition *)
Class Eq (A : Type) := {
  eqb : A -> A -> bool;
  eqb_correct : forall x y, eqb x y = true <-> x = y
}.

(* Instance for nat *)
Instance NatEq : Eq nat := {
  eqb := Nat.eqb;
  eqb_correct := Nat.eqb_eq
}.

(* Generic function using the type class *)
Definition elem {A : Type} `{Eq A} (x : A) (l : list A) : bool :=
  existsb (eqb x) l.

Compute elem 3 [1;2;3;4].  (* = true *)
```

Type classes in Coq use `Class`/`Instance` and backtick syntax `` `{Eq A} `` for implicit class constraints. They work via **instance search** — Coq finds the right instance automatically.
